 "note": "Per-genre verifier agreement on ANLI's verified subset. gold_majority_rate = share of a genre's examples whose writer gold equals the strict verifier majority; gold_support_rate = fraction of that genre's individual verifier votes that equal the writer gold (a continuous decisiveness measure, defined for k=2 and k=3 lines alike). by_genre pools across rounds (confounded with the adversary round, since 5 of 6 genres are R3-only); by_genre_r3 holds the round fixed at R3. P1 (structural, finding either way) bets gold == strict majority on >99% of examples in EVERY genre (gold derivation robust to domain). P2 (directional, finding either way) bets that WITHIN R3 the gold-support rate still varies across genres by >0.03, so text domain predicts verifier decisiveness even at a single adversary round. P3 (cross-check) bets gold == strict majority on 29,765 of 29,803 joined lines (reproduces audits 39/48). Compare pooled_support_rate with r3_support_rate for any Simpson's-paradox reordering once the round is controlled."
